.141176 .211765 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 28 290 Tm (The Riverview-Mill District Mobility & Connectivity Plan is a fictional planning exercise demonstrating how a neighborhood transportation strategy can connect residents to jobs, transit, parks and daily) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 28 279.2 Tm (needs without requiring a private automobile. The district is close to major destinations, but long crossings, incomplete bicycle facilities, uneven transit access, an inactive rail corridor and winter) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 28 268.4 Tm (maintenance gaps make short trips difficult or unreliable.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 9.6 TL ET
.141176 .211765 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 28 253.6 Tm (The recommended network combines a complete-street transformation on Maple Avenue, a 2.4-mile Foundry rail-trail greenway, safer crossings, first- and last-mile transit improvements, park connections) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 28 242.8 Tm (and public-realm investments. Each recommendation addresses a different point in the same trip, so the plan emphasizes continuity rather than isolated projects.) Tj T* ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 9.6 TL ET
.141176 .211765 .239216 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 28 228 Tm (Implementation is phased so quick-build safety work and design can begin before larger capital projects. Physical improvements are paired with transit operations, winter maintenance and employer) Tj T* ET
BT 1 0 0 1 28 217.2 Tm (coordination. Performance measures track employment access, low-stress network proximity, accessible-route continuity and resident-reported crossing comfort.) Tj T* ET
